		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Re: Hotspot with DM1801: HD1 with a bad tx quality]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2099&amp;p=17460#p17460"><![CDATA[
Hi,<br><blockquote class="uncited"><div>Good evening to all.<br>I hope this would be the right section for my post. <br>As wrote on Subject i've got a boring issue with my new Ailunce HD1 GPS when i use it on my hotspot using a Baofeng DM1801 with OpenGD77 fw and a Pi-Star on Raspberry Pi3: who heard me tells that my modulation is so close, saturated, sometimes i lose some packet, simply it's very difficult and annoying to listen my talk. I can see a BER over 5%/6%, that's is so strange because with other radios there's no problem, no loss, no BER over 1, a great modulation; moreover HD1 works properly in other hotspots (tried with a GD77, with a MMDVM board on Pi-star and with 2 repeters) so i thought there's something like incompatibility between DM1801 (in HS mode) and this HD1. I hope i've explained all clearly despite my poor english. So, does anybody had same issues and could me take some opinion?<br>Thanks to all and 73</div></blockquote>I would like to see the MMDVMHost log after "bad quality" transmission (you have a download button in the PiStar's "Live Logs" tab in the web interface).<br>Also, you may check the HD1's hotspot channel configuration, maybe it's related to a wrong setting, as you wrote that it works correctly with other radios.<br>Or the radio (HD1) is a bit off frequency.<br><br>Cheers.<br>---<br>Daniel<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=56">F1RMB</a> — Sun Feb 13, 2022 7:08 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
